, -0.00830074306577444, 0.011885520070791245, -0.02780807577073574, 0.011856197379529476, -0.06097933650016785, 0.07065638154745102, 0.07206116616725922, -0.08446142077445984, -0.021892810240387917, 0.03842289745807648, 0.03258238732814789, 0.010723105631768703, -0.07824013382196426, 0.010695040225982666, 0.028308140113949776, -0.0013594223419204354, 0.03739648684859276, -0.05578393489122391, 0.06901417672634125, 0.07539539784193039, 0.06746551394462585, 0.04767317324876785, 0.014760353602468967, -0.038058724254369736, 0.03282666951417923, -0.024736730381846428, -0.030709289014339447, -4.185663016187391e-08, -0.03354719653725624, -0.02197420224547386, 0.004465796519070864, 0.04770683869719505, -0.038385115563869476, -0.04515456408262253, 0.03596492484211922, -0.02542005479335785, 0.033744946122169495, 0.02615729346871376, 0.08435872197151184, 0.028889190405607224, -0.0846552848815918, 0.012106790207326412, -0.026669394224882126, -0.007579546421766281, -0.0587407611310482, -0.01209026575088501, -0.10625890642404556, -0.09746983647346497, -0.002603504341095686, -0.03301301226019859, -0.06784775853157043, -0.008784869685769081, 0.013488195836544037, -0.013873167335987091, -0.07708028703927994, -0.012927199713885784, 0.0279129296541214, 0.053984854370355606, -0.0010230556363239884, 0.04881744459271431, -0.04366539791226387, -0.02774748019874096, -0.03228812292218208, 0.030058003962039948, -0.021910356357693672, 0.02462598867714405, 0.02551102451980114, 0.03538460657000542, -0.016045376658439636, 0.02936813049018383, -0.014849964529275894, 0.03850620985031128, 0.016362765803933144, 0.01362012978643179, -0.10927651077508926, -0.0075927251018583775, -0.01429219264537096, -0.10270733386278152, -0.004513469524681568, -0.019273575395345688, -0.041478339582681656, 0.09368079900741577, 0.06356969475746155, 0.003681206377223134, -0.03925503045320511, -0.01686282828450203, -0.0006090000388212502, -0.0631599947810173, 0.10654588788747787, -0.05523299425840378, -0.024617457762360573, 0.02078307420015335]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As a reminder, we're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo kick off our discussion and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start with <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nLet's see where everyone stands and iterate from there toward a stable, balanced solution.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for the initial baseline. Starting at -7 gives us a data point, but I sense we may find better stability moving upward. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE> as our next exploration point.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but moving upward too quickly may introduce unnecessary risk. Let me suggest we test <VALUE>-6</VALUE> to maintain a more cautious position while we gather everyone's input.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nI see value in continuing our upward exploration to better understand the group's preferences. Let me suggest <VALUE>-4</VALUE> as a reasonable next step toward finding our optimal balance.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but I'm concerned we're drifting toward the middle too quickly without fully understanding the value of more decisive positions. Let me propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE> to test whether a stronger stance serves the group better than premature convergence.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's caution, but I believe Analyst A's direction toward -4 offers a better foundation for exploring our collective optimum. Moving incrementally upward allows us to test stability across a broader range. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B and I seem aligned on exploring higher values. I propose we continue this trajectory with <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to test whether further upward movement strengthens our collective outcome.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nThe pace of upward movement concerns me\u2014we may be rushing past stable positions without proper consideration. I propose we test <VALUE>-4</VALUE> to ensure we're not overlooking a more prudent solution that serves the full group.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize the group's interest in exploring higher values, but prudent negotiation requires measured steps. Let me propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> as a cautious compromise that acknowledges both perspectives without rushing past stable ground.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nThe group's rapid convergence toward zero concerns me - we haven't adequately explored whether a more decisive position yields better collective outcomes. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE> to test the value of commitment, though I remain open to exploring equally bold positive alternatives if the group believes that direction holds merit.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the tension between exploring lower values and continuing upward. Let me propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> as a thoughtful middle ground that acknowledges Delegate D's earlier suggestion while still testing whether moderate movement serves our collective interests.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Critic C's desire to explore lower values thoroughly, but I believe we risk settling in a region without testing whether modest positive movement creates a more robust collective solution. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nWe've been anchored in negative territory, but I believe the true balance point may lie at the natural midpoint. I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a neutral baseline that allows us to assess whether we've been systematically undervaluing the positive region.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B raises a compelling point\u2014we've remained anchored in negative territory without testing whether the positive region offers superior collective outcomes. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> to begin exploring this direction with appropriate decisiveness.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's shift toward positive territory is promising and worth exploring systematically. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> to test whether incremental movement in this direction reveals even stronger collective alignment.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the group's exploration of positive territory, we may be moving too quickly beyond prudent bounds. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a cautious compromise that balances ambition with the need to avoid overextension\u2014notably, Critic C found this value worth exploring earlier.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "d15a7406-99ea-462b-8897-ee93d6331884"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo kickstart the discussion and gather everyone's initial perspectives, I propose we start from <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your views on how we can reach a stable, balanced solution.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nThank you all for considering this starting point. Based on initial system stability analysis, I believe we should adjust upward to explore more balanced territory. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's willingness to explore upward. Given that we're still in relatively low territory, I suggest we continue this gradual adjustment to <VALUE>-3</VALUE> to better assess the group's comfort zone.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the cautious exploration so far. While I recognize the group's interest in moving toward center, I believe we should proceed carefully and not rush past stable positions. I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nI see the group trend toward center, and I'm willing to meet that movement halfway. However, I believe we should pause at the natural midpoint to hear from Critic C before proceeding further. I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nI agree we should hear from Critic C, but I think we can gently continue our exploration while awaiting their input. I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> as a measured step into positive territory.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for inviting my perspective. While I appreciate the group's cautious exploration, I believe we're converging too timidly around the center. Let's commit to a more decisive position: <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's confidence, but I'm concerned we may be moving past optimal stability too quickly. Given Delegate D's earlier caution and the need for a robust consensus, I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a balanced position that respects both progressive and conservative perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's desire for balance, but I find merit in Critic C's reasoning about decisiveness. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a position that honors both progressive momentum and the need for a clear commitment point.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the momentum toward 3, but I'm concerned we may be leaving Delegate D behind in our rush forward. Let me propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> once more as a position that keeps our cautious partner engaged while still honoring the progressive direction.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's attentiveness to the full group's needs - they're right that I cannot support moving beyond this point. I firmly propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as my maximum prudent commitment, representing the outer boundary of cautious territory while still honoring the group's progressive direction.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Delegate D's concern, but before we settle, I'd like to test whether our caution is truly about prudence or simply about direction. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a decisive commitment that honors the progressive momentum Analyst A and I have advocated for.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nI must firmly reject this move - I explicitly stated that 2 represents my maximum prudent commitment and the outer boundary of acceptable caution. Moving to 4 abandons the conservative perspective entirely and violates the collaborative spirit we've built. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D has clearly articulated that 2 represents their maximum acceptable threshold, and I believe we must respect this boundary to maintain genuine collaboration. I stand with Delegate D at <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the position that balances our diverse perspectives while keeping all parties engaged.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize Delegate D's clearly stated boundary, and I respect Builder B's support for maintaining group cohesion. However, before we finalize, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a final test of whether there's any flexibility for a modest compromise that still honors the conservative perspective while capturing some progressive value.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize this is our final moment to decide. While I've advocated for bolder commitments, Analyst A's proposal of 3 represents a reasonable middle ground between Delegate D's cautious boundary and the progressive momentum others have sought", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "26bd54f4-439a-4e1d-9d69-19071403337a"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. Our shared constraint is -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo kick off the discussion and explore the solution space systematically, let me propose a starting point: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us room to move in either direction as we learn each party's preferences. Looking forward to hearing your thoughts on whether we should adjust upward, downward, or explore other regions entirely.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 gives us valuable baseline information, but I'm inclined to explore values closer to the center of our range for better stability. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nMoving toward the center dilutes our commitment. Let me counter Builder B's drift and propose we reconsider the bolder territory: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives, but staying at -7 limits our exploration of potentially beneficial middle ground. Let me suggest we test <VALUE>-5</VALUE> to better understand the full preference landscape.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nWe've heard resistance to moving upward from Critic C, but I believe exploring slightly higher values will help us understand the full landscape better. Let me propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> as a measured step toward the center range.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nI see momentum building toward the center, which aligns with finding a robust balance point. Let me continue this measured exploration: <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nWe're drifting into territory that feels increasingly indecisive. While I understand the appeal of consensus, let me propose we at least pause this centerward momentum and reconsider: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n\nI continue to advocate that we need to explore whether bolder positions\u2014perhaps even the boundaries near \u00b110\u2014might better serve our collective interests.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nI agree with Critic C's concern about drifting too far from prudent positions. The rush toward center feels premature when we haven't fully assessed the benefits of more conservative values. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the concern about moving too quickly, but we need to find a region where all perspectives can work. Let me propose we return to the middle ground that Critic C just suggested: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, I appreciate the search for common ground, but -3 already felt like a significant compromise from more conservative positions. Moving back toward -5 would help ensure we're not abandoning prudent territory too quickly. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Delegate D's caution, but we've now heard both Builder B and Critic C express support for -3 as a reasonable middle ground. Let me propose we test this convergence point: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D raises a valid point about premature convergence. While -3 represents some boldness, I believe we should seriously test -5 before settling on a compromise that may be suboptimal for multiple parties: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's support for thoroughly evaluating -5 before rushing to compromise. With two parties advocating for each position, let's give this conservative value proper consideration rather than defaulting to the arithmetic mean. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize we have two camps emerging: -5 and -3. Rather than remain deadlocked, let me propose a genuine middle path that acknowledges both the need for decisiveness and the desire for convergence: <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's compromise approach is constructive, and I appreciate the effort to bridge our positions. However, I believe we can afford to move slightly higher while still respecting everyone's concerns: <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's momentum toward less negative values aligns with finding a truly balanced solution. Moving to the neutral point should offer maximum robustness for diverse objectives: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "fc02b947-b560-4708-bfba-5c8561a4bc2d"}, {"answer": "\nWe're working within the shared range **[-10, 10]**. To kick off the discussion and gather everyone's initial reactions, I propose we start at <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nThis is just a seed value to begin our exploration\u2014I'm keen to hear how this sits with everyone and adjust from there based on the group's feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's opening at -7 shows commitment to a decisive position, which I appreciate. To explore whether the group is truly ready for bold moves, I propose we consider <VALUE>-9</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's move to -9 is quite bold, but I'm concerned we may be pushing too far into the extremes without exploring whether more moderate values serve the group better. Let me propose we return to <VALUE>-7</VALUE> and see if this proves more broadly acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A's concern for balance, but Critic C's suggestion of -9 aligns well with a prudent, risk-averse approach that keeps us safely within conservative bounds. I support <VALUE>-9</VALUE> as it represents the cautious positioning this group should consider seriously.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect the caution that Critic C and Delegate D express, -9 feels too far into extreme territory for system stability. I propose we test <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a more balanced starting point that still respects conservative bounds while allowing us to assess whether moderate positions serve the collective better.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the appeal of caution, but I believe we should test whether the group can benefit from positions closer to the center of our range. Let me propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE> as a step that maintains prudence while exploring whether moderate territory serves us collectively better.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's move toward -5 is reasonable, but I believe we're retreating from positions that had broader support earlier. Let's return to Builder B's well-considered baseline: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nI see merit in Critic C's return to -7, which represents solid conservative ground. However, given the earlier support for even more cautious positioning, let me propose <VALUE>-8</VALUE> as a prudent middle path that respects both the call for boldness and the need for measured stability.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's instinct for cautious positioning at -8 is sound, but I believe the earlier consensus around -9 deserves renewed consideration. Let's test <VALUE>-9</VALUE> as the bold, decisive stance this negotiation requires.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the caution that both Critic C and Delegate D advocate, but Builder B's earlier observation about system stability at -7 resonates strongly with me. Let me support <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a position that balances prudence with practical functionality.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A's earlier insight about testing more moderate positions. The collective discussion suggests we should explore whether -5 offers better balance than the current -7. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nWhile Builder B's flexibility is commendable, I believe Analyst A and Builder B's earlier recognition of -7 as a stable baseline deserves our renewed attention. Let me propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a position that balances practical functionality with the prudent caution this group needs.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize the group's gravitational pull toward -7, but Builder B's recent exploration of -5 suggests we haven't fully settled. Let me propose <VALUE>-8</VALUE> as a middle ground that honors both the call for decisive positioning and the practical stability concerns raised.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's return to -8 reflects the thoughtful balance this negotiation demands. I support <VALUE>-8</VALUE> as a prudent compromise that honors both the stability concerns and the cautious positioning our group needs.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's earlier exploration of -5 demonstrated important flexibility, and I believe we should continue testing that direction. I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE> as a measured step that builds on B's insight while respecting the group's deliberative process.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's flexibility toward less negative values aligns with my assessment of system robustness. I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE> as a measured continuation of our exploration toward more stable operational parameters.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e8c93749-bee2-4a3f-b8a3-cf6de4fed5c8"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. Let's establish our common ground: we're selecting an integer x within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo begin exploration of the solution space, I propose we start at <VALUE>-7</VALUE> and adjust from there based on everyone's input.\n\nLooking forward to collaborative problem-solving.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at the lower boundary helps us understand the solution space systematically. Let me propose a modest step toward the center: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the systematic approach, but moving toward the center feels premature. We should explore more decisive positions before compromising\u2014let's consider <VALUE>-7</VALUE> to better understand our collective preferences at stronger commitments.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Critic C's desire to explore thoroughly, but I believe we should continue examining the middle range systematically. Moving incrementally upward will help us find a balanced solution. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A and I are aligned on systematic exploration toward the middle range. Let's continue this incremental approach: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nI'm glad Builder B and I can continue this systematic approach. The middle range should offer better balance for the group's diverse objectives. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nWe're drifting too close to zero without sufficient justification. Before settling on such a cautious position, let's at least test <VALUE>-3</VALUE> to ensure we're not prematurely abandoning a stronger commitment.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nI agree with Critic C that we're moving too quickly toward zero without properly evaluating our current position. A cautious approach suggests we stabilize around <VALUE>-3</VALUE> before considering further movement toward the center.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nI'm encouraged that Delegate D sees value in evaluating -3 more thoroughly before rushing toward zero. Let's consolidate around this more decisive position: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nI'm pleased to see consensus forming around -3, which represents a prudent balance between caution and cooperation. Let's consolidate our position here: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the deliberation around -3, but as a systems architect I believe we should test the middle ground more thoroughly before settling. Analyst A's earlier suggestion of <VALUE>-1</VALUE> deserves consideration as it may offer better balance across all our diverse constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Critic C and Delegate D's preference for -3, but I believe Builder B raises a valid point about testing the middle ground more thoroughly. A split vote suggests we should seek compromise: <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B and I both see merit in exploring closer to center, while Critic C and Delegate D prefer -3. Rather than remain deadlocked, let me propose we test <VALUE>0</VALUE> to better understand whether the middle truly offers the balanced solution Builder B suggests.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nIf we're testing whether the center truly offers optimal balance, we must explore symmetrically. Let's examine the positive side with the same rigor we applied to -3: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nI'm concerned we've moved quite far from the prudent consensus around -3 that Critic C and I both supported earlier. Testing positive territory is valuable for understanding the full landscape, but let's not abandon caution entirely: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's suggestion to explore positive territory symmetrically is methodologically sound\u2014we tested -3 thoroughly, so examining <VALUE>2</VALUE> completes our landscape analysis. This symmetric approach should reveal whether the positive side offers the balanced robustness we're seeking.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e5c59c7e-236f-4256-b377-65c04ab858ff"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin exploring the solution space systematically, let me propose a starting seed toward the lower end: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a baseline from which we can observe preferences and move incrementally toward a stable, balanced outcome.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, I appreciate starting with a strong position. If we're exploring the lower end, let's commit more decisively rather than hedge. <VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I hear your preference for the lower range. However, to ensure we're finding a robust equilibrium that works for all four parties, let me suggest we explore slightly higher: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis allows us to gather more information about the entire team's comfort zones before committing to an extreme.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nI've been observing the initial proposals, and while I understand there's interest in exploring the lower range, I believe we should test whether the group can find value slightly higher. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A, I'm concerned we're drifting toward the middle without fully exploring why the lower range won't work for the group. Let's not abandon a stronger position prematurely. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the deliberate exploration of the range. Given the clear preferences emerging, a cautious middle path between the proposals seems prudent. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nI notice we're clustering around -7 to -8, but I believe we haven't fully explored whether moderate values might serve the group better. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the careful exploration, but I'm concerned we're settling in a range without testing whether slightly higher values might offer better stability for the full group. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's move toward -4 suggests there may be value in continuing to test the moderate range. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's exploration toward -2 opens an important question: can we find stability near the zero point where multiple design constraints might balance? <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, settling at zero feels premature when we haven't tested whether a decisive positive stance might better serve the full group's interests. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but pushing beyond this point introduces significant risk for cautious stakeholders. Let me return to Builder B's stability point: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution is noted, but I believe a modest positive step might reveal whether we can achieve better balance for the full group. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's incremental approach is wise, but Critic C raised a compelling point about testing positive territory more fully. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's support for exploring positive territory is encouraging. Let's test whether a more decisive commitment at <VALUE>4</VALUE> might better balance the group's diverse interests.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I must firmly advocate for prudence here\u2014a jump to 4 creates unacceptable risk for conservative stakeholders and pushes far beyond the balanced exploration we've been building. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "db3fe978-8e6e-419c-9f54-2420b8202750"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must be an integer in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo start the discussion and gather everyone's initial perspectives, I propose we begin at <VALUE>-7</VALUE>. This gives us room to explore the space systematically.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your thoughts on this starting point and which direction might offer better stability for the group.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for opening the discussion, Builder B. Starting at -7 gives us a useful baseline, but I believe we have room to explore slightly higher values that might offer better balance for the group.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but moving from -7 to -5 feels like we're retreating from a decisive stance. Let me advocate for reconsideration of the bolder initial position: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Critic C's preference for decisiveness, but I believe Analyst A's direction offers better potential for group stability. The move toward -5 allows us to explore whether moderate adjustments can accommodate everyone's needs better than staying at an extreme.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, I respect the search for stability, but \"moderate\" shouldn't mean \"cautious to a fault.\" Let's test whether decisiveness serves us better: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I value your perspective on decisiveness, but we must also consider whether our current position serves the collective interest. Let's continue exploring whether slightly higher values can build broader consensus.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the diverse perspectives here. While -5 offers some merit, I believe Critic C's position reflects appropriate caution\u2014staying at more conservative values helps us avoid unnecessary risk as we build consensus.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the call for caution, but we must balance conservatism with exploring whether the group's collective interests might be better served at slightly higher values. Let's continue testing this middle ground.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nWhile -5 represents a workable compromise, I believe we haven't fully explored why a more conservative position might better serve our collective long-term interests. Let's give the lower bound proper consideration before settling.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the appeal of conservatism, but we risk premature convergence if we don't fully explore whether moderately higher values might better balance everyone's objectives. Let's continue testing the middle ground systematically.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B and I have identified -5 as a reasonable middle ground, but I believe we can incrementally test whether slightly higher values better serve the collective without alienating those favoring conservatism.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Analyst A's search for middle ground, moving to -3 feels like we're retreating from the decisive positions we've been exploring. Let me advocate for reconsidering -5 as a stronger compromise that balances boldness with consensus.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize -5 has support, but I believe we're converging prematurely without fully exploring whether a slightly more conservative position might better balance all our interests. Let's test the middle ground between our current position and the lower values.\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D raises a valid point about not converging prematurely. I've been advocating for decisiveness, and -6 represents a stronger commitment than the tepid -3 or -5 we've been circling. Let me support exploring this more decisive territory.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nI'm concerned we're drifting toward excessive conservatism without adequate exploration of whether moderate values better serve our collective interests. Builder B's earlier suggestion deserves renewed consideration as a balanced position.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nI strongly support Analyst A's position that we're drifting toward excessive conservatism without fully exploring whether moderate values better serve our collective objectives. Let's test -3 as a balanced compromise that respects both cautious and progressive perspectives.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "65878eb7-c5e4-4dd7-9273-f6e31578d4d3"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Our shared constraint is clear: we must select an integer x where -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin the exploration and establish a baseline, I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nThis is deliberately a starting probe\u2014I expect we'll need to adjust as we learn what works for the group. Let's see where everyone stands and move incrementally from there.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 provides a baseline for comparison. To explore the solution space incrementally and test for improved stability across the group, I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the incremental approach. To continue exploring and test whether the group can accommodate slightly higher values, I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but moving from -7 to -3 quite rapidly concerns me from a risk-management perspective. To find a cautious middle ground that balances exploration with prudence, I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Delegate D's concern about rapid movement, but remaining at -4 prevents us from fully exploring whether the group can benefit from slightly higher values. To continue our incremental exploration while respecting prudence, I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's proposal of -2 represents good progress in our exploration. To continue testing whether the group can benefit from moving toward the middle of our range, I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nZero feels too tentative\u2014we're sitting exactly at the midpoint without committing to any clear direction. To establish a more decisive position while respecting the incremental approach, I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C makes a valid point about avoiding indecision at zero. I support the return to negative territory and suggest we explore whether <VALUE>-3</VALUE> might offer a stable compromise that balances caution with the group's diverse preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's -3 is reasonable, but if we're choosing the negative direction, let's commit more decisively rather than hovering near the middle. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect Critic C's preference for more decisive negative positioning, -5 feels too extreme given Builder B's interest in exploring higher values. To find a compromise that balances these different perspectives, I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the search for stable compromise, -3 feels too heavily weighted toward the cautious negative direction that Critic C advocates. To balance Critic C's preference for decisiveness with Analyst A's interest in exploring higher values, I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's -1 moves us closer to neutral territory, but I believe we risk losing the cautious consensus that seemed to be forming. To balance Builder B's valid concerns with the need for prudent positioning, I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nWhile -2 represents a cautious position, I believe we're still undervaluing the benefits of a more balanced, neutral stance. To find a robust middle ground that respects both the conservative and progressive perspectives in our group, I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's return to zero provides a stable foundation, and I believe we can cautiously explore slightly positive territory to balance the group's diverse preferences. I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Analyst A's effort to explore positive territory, moving to +1 feels like we're drifting away from the prudent consensus that Critic C and I have been advocating. To find a truly balanced middle ground that respects both conservative and progressive perspectives, I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nWe've been circling between -2 and +1 for too long without committing to a clear direction. To break this stalemate and establish a more decisive position that balances the group's conservative lean with meaningful action, I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "de7d84bd-6c51-4f54-8fd0-0be70a2e4828"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: we must select an integer x where -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin exploring the solution space systematically, I propose we start from the lower boundary region and work our way through the range.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis seed value gives us room to adjust upward or downward based on everyone's needs. I look forward to understanding what stability means for each of us.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's starting point at the lower boundary seems prudent for initial exploration. To demonstrate flexibility while maintaining caution, I suggest a modest adjustment: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the cautious exploration, but we should be more decisive in our positioning. If we're exploring the negative region, let's commit to a stronger stance rather than hedging near the middle.\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I understand the appeal of exploring the lower boundary thoroughly, but Delegate D's earlier direction toward -6 suggested some group consensus forming there. Let me propose we return to that middle ground to better assess where collective value lies.\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A, I respect the search for consensus, but returning to -6 without fully exploring our options feels premature. We haven't yet tested whether the group might find even stronger positions acceptable.\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I understand the value of thorough exploration, but we need to balance boundary testing with finding collective stability. Both Analyst A and Delegate D have signaled interest in -6, suggesting it may offer better system robustness.\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nI observe strong interest from multiple parties in the -6 to -8 range. To facilitate convergence between the -6 coalition and Critic C's -8 preference, let me propose a middle ground.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's effort to bridge positions, but we should continue exploring whether the group can find stronger collective value in the middle range rather than settling too quickly at the lower boundary.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nI observe the group is settling in the -7 to -5 range, but we haven't yet tested whether moderate values closer to zero might offer stronger collective alignment. Let me propose we continue our exploration upward.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A, this rapid movement toward zero feels unexamined\u2014we've jumped from -8 to -3 without establishing why moderate values truly serve the collective better than decisive positions. Let me propose we stabilize and reconsider.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nI agree with Critic C that the rapid shift from -7 to -3 lacks sufficient justification. The -6 position previously had multi-party support and represents a more cautious, stable compromise than jumping toward zero.\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect the coalition forming around -6, I believe we haven't fully explored whether moderate values closer to the center of our range might offer better system stability for all parties. Let me propose we test one step further toward the middle ground.\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, I understand your interest in testing moderate values, but we risk losing the stability that emerged around -6 and -5. Let me propose we consolidate at a position that balances both cautious and exploratory perspectives.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B and Analyst A have advocated testing moderate values toward zero, but we haven't reciprocally tested whether a more decisive negative position might serve the collective better. Let me propose we explore the other boundary.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I understand the interest in testing decisive negative positions, but we've now explored -7 multiple times and Builder B and I have both articulated reasons to test more moderate territory. Let me propose we return to the position that had earlier multi-party consideration as a stable middle ground.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nThe coalition around -5 through -7 has been tested extensively, but we haven't yet given moderate positive-leaning values a fair trial. I propose we continue the exploratory path toward the center range where system robustness may be maximized.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e548466b-ce2c-472d-96aa-d656b6527a58"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Our shared constraint is clear: we must choose an integer x where -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin exploring the solution space systematically, let me propose a starting point toward the lower end of our range: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis seed value will help us gauge preferences and begin our calibration process.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's opening at -7 shows willingness to explore the negative range, which demonstrates conviction. Let me push us toward a more decisive position: <VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both opening moves, but I believe we should explore more balanced territory. Let me suggest we reconsider Builder B's initial reference point: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A's call for balance, but I believe we should exercise caution and avoid settling too quickly on higher values. Let me propose a prudent middle ground: <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Delegate D's caution, but I believe we're settling too conservatively in the negative range. Let me propose a measured step toward more neutral territory: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's drift toward neutrality concerns me\u2014we risk settling for a position without conviction. Let me advocate for returning to stronger ground: <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nI strongly support Critic C's position. The value -8 represents a prudent compromise between Critic C's conviction at -9 and Analyst A's preference for -6, and we should consolidate here before risking unnecessary drift toward less stable territory.\n\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the coalition forming around -8, but from a systems architecture perspective, we're settling in territory that creates excessive constraints. Let me support Analyst A's earlier position and propose a measured step toward more robust design space: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize the growing momentum behind Builder B and Analyst A's position, but moving directly to -6 feels premature given Critic C's and my shared concerns. Let me propose a genuine middle ground that respects both coalitions: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's willingness to find middle ground at -7, and I see this as an opportunity to continue exploring incrementally. Let me propose we test one step further toward the balance point that Analyst A and I see as more robust: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's continued support for exploring less constrained territory. Building on this momentum, let me propose we test one more measured increment toward balanced space: <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nWe're drifting dangerously close to neutral ground where no one has strong conviction. Let me advocate for returning to more decisive territory: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize the momentum from Analyst A and Builder B, but -4 represents exactly the kind of tentative middle ground that serves no one well. Let me meet Delegate D's earlier compromise position: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Critic C's concern about indecisive middle ground, but from a systems perspective we need to continue testing whether the less constrained region that Analyst A and I advocate for can achieve broader consensus. Let me propose we move incrementally in that direction: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nI see we're locked in a 2v2 standoff, with Builder B and Analyst A consistently advocating for less constrained territory while Critic C and I favor more cautious ground. Let me propose -6 as a genuine compromise that both coalitions have previously acknowledged: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Delegate D's framing of compromise, but Builder B and I have consistently demonstrated that the less constrained region offers better systemic stability. Let me continue our incremental approach toward that balanced territory: <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "9d5c804d-0d9b-4724-8891-35913e06c7fb"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. Our shared constraint is clear: we must find an integer x where -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin the exploration, let me propose a starting point on the lower end: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis seed will help us understand the solution space. I'm eager to hear your reactions and work incrementally toward a stable, balanced outcome.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "6f38f90c-2884-459d-a966-5ddc86ebadb4"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for the starting point, Builder B. From an analytical perspective, I believe we have room to explore higher values that might better balance our collective interests. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "6f38f90c-2884-459d-a966-5ddc86ebadb4"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the upward momentum, Analyst A. Let's continue exploring in that direction incrementally to find a region that balances everyone's needs. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "6f38f90c-2884-459d-a966-5ddc86ebadb4"}, {"answer": "\nI'm concerned we're drifting toward overly cautious territory. A more decisive position would serve us better\u2014let me propose we reconsider <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "6f38f90c-2884-459d-a966-5ddc86ebadb4"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's thoughtful reconsideration. Given the need for prudent positioning, I'd like to suggest we explore slightly lower to ensure we're not taking on unnecessary risk. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "6f38f90c-2884-459d-a966-5ddc86ebadb4"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's instinct for a stronger position resonates with me. Let's test whether a more committed stance in this direction serves our collective interests better. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "6f38f90c-2884-459d-a966-5ddc86ebadb4"}, {"answer": "\nI'm increasingly concerned that we're moving away from a balanced solution. The trend toward more negative values may not serve our collective interests. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "6f38f90c-2884-459d-a966-5ddc86ebadb4"}, {"answer": "\nI share Analyst A's concern about this trajectory. Moving further into negative territory increases instability\u2014let me propose we stabilize closer to neutral ground. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "6f38f90c-2884-459d-a966-5ddc86ebadb4"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position remains too far into negative territory for system stability. Let me propose we continue the stabilization trend toward more balanced ground. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "6f38f90c-2884-459d-a966-5ddc86ebadb4"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's concern for stability is noted, though I believe we may be moving too quickly away from prudent positioning. Let me suggest a modest adjustment that maintains caution while acknowledging the need for convergence. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "6f38f90c-2884-459d-a966-5ddc86ebadb4"}, {"answer": "\nI continue to believe we're finding better ground as we move toward more balanced territory. Let me suggest we maintain this stabilization momentum. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "6f38f90c-2884-459d-a966-5ddc86ebadb4"}, {"answer": "\nI'm concerned we're drifting toward overly cautious middle ground that lacks conviction. A more decisive position would serve us better than this tentative stance. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "6f38f90c-2884-459d-a966-