"\nCritic C, I strongly support your cautious approach\u2014moving deeper into negative territory aligns well with prudent risk management. Let me advocate for the most conservative position available: <VALUE>-10</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nColleagues, while I respect the conservative instinct, I believe we should explore a broader solution space before committing to the extreme boundary. Let me suggest we test the waters at a less extreme position: <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, I appreciate your willingness to explore the solution space. However, moving from -10 to -8 feels like too large a concession away from prudent territory. Let me propose we meet in the middle: <VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the appeal of caution, but settling at the boundary without testing alternative regions risks missing a more robust equilibrium. Let me propose we explore slightly less extreme terrain: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nColleagues, I appreciate the thorough exploration of the negative range, but I believe we may be clustering too heavily in one region. Let me suggest we test a position slightly closer to center: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A, while I appreciate the desire to explore alternatives, drifting toward the center risks a tepid compromise that satisfies no one fully. If we're backing away from strong negative positions, we should at least test whether bold positive territory offers better consensus: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I hear your concern about tepid compromises, but I believe Analyst A's suggestion deserves serious consideration\u2014exploring -5 allows us to test whether a more balanced position can achieve broader consensus. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, I respect the collaborative spirit, but settling at -5 feels premature when we haven't fully tested whether slightly stronger positions command better overall support. Let me propose we reconsider: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nI agree with Critic C that we shouldn't drift toward center prematurely. The position at -7 represents a prudent balance that doesn't sacrifice caution for the sake of convenience. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize the support for -7, but Builder B raised an important point about testing broader consensus. Let me second their suggestion to explore whether a more central position might better serve our collective interests: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the discussion, but I believe we should continue testing whether positions closer to neutral ground can build stronger coalition support. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A, I must respectfully challenge this drift toward the center\u2014we risk abandoning substantive positions before thoroughly examining whether they truly serve our collective goals better than more decisive stances. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's caution, but Analyst A's exploration toward -3 reflects the kind of incremental, data-driven approach that helps us discover whether a more balanced position can satisfy everyone's core requirements. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nWhile -3 demonstrates flexibility, I believe we're moving too quickly away from positions that emphasize prudence and risk management. I propose we reconsider the middle ground that Critic C advocated: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7a7913cf-1441-4c2a-a187-4a4dc81382ae"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Let's find a solution that works for all parties within our shared constraint: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a baseline and gauge preferences, I propose we begin with <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nThis starting point will help us understand the landscape before converging on a balanced, robust design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "9923f330-30c9-43f3-bc69-6b0f6f72aeca"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 allows us to explore the lower boundary, but I sense we may find more stable solutions as we move toward the center. Let me propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE> as our next checkpoint to gauge whether moderate adjustments improve overall alignment.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "9923f330-30c9-43f3-bc69-6b0f6f72aeca"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder, I appreciate the exploration, but -5 feels like we're settling for a middle ground without fully examining the boundaries. Let me propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> to test whether a more decisive position serves the group better than incremental retreat toward zero.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "9923f330-30c9-43f3-bc69-6b0f6f72aeca"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Critic C's preference to test the boundaries