about thorough evaluation, but the structural indicators suggest we should continue our systematic exploration toward the center where robustness metrics typically improve. I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> as a measured step that respects both caution and forward progress.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "9923f330-30c9-43f3-bc69-6b0f6f72aeca"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's structural logic resonates strongly - the pattern suggests we should continue this measured progression toward the center. I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE> as the natural next checkpoint in our systematic exploration, allowing us to evaluate whether this central position offers the balanced configuration we're seeking.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "9923f330-30c9-43f3-bc69-6b0f6f72aeca"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A, while zero represents a theoretical midpoint, we shouldn't settle for the center without exploring whether a more committed stance yields better outcomes. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> to test the positive direction symmetrically and ensure we're making an informed decision rather than defaulting to apparent neutrality.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "9923f330-30c9-43f3-bc69-6b0f6f72aeca"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, while I appreciate the exploration of positive territory, we must recognize that moving beyond the center carries significant risk for more conservative stakeholders. I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE> as the true neutral position that balances all perspectives without pushing too far into uncertain territory.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "9923f330-30c9-43f3-bc69-6b0f6f72aeca"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C raises a valid point about exploring positive territory symmetrically before settling on zero. I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> as a measured compromise that tests the positive direction while respecting Delegate D's caution about moving too aggressively beyond center.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round